{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39499460",
      "title": "The Query Configuration Object & Aborting Requests",
      "sourceHash": "612d5149c80260a9a7189e82f94f462cc735ff2e4e61dafb541a0d15079c3df9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 2.76,
          "en": "So why is search term",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 5.087,
          "en": "set to some strange value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.087,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "as we can see in this one request here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "when the new events section component tries to fetch events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 14.103,
          "en": "with this useQuery usage?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 17.28,
          "en": "Well, because React Query",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.28,
          "end": 22.28,
          "en": "and the useQuery hook actually passes some default data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.751,
          "end": 26.14,
          "en": "to this Query function you're defining here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.27,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "and we can see that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 32.793,
          "en": "if we simply console log search term here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 38.46,
          "en": "If we do that, we should see two logs in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.46,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "because we got two components, the find events section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 44.22,
          "en": "and the new events section components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.22,
          "end": 48.423,
          "en": "that do use the fetch events function with React Query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "So if I go back and I reload here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 58.2,
          "en": "I do see two results here, but they're pretty strange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.2,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "The second result is empty, an empty string essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 65.80199999999999,
          "en": "But the first result is an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.80199999999999,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "An object which I never passed to fetch events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 72.434,
          "en": "in no place of this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.434,
          "end": 74.787,
          "en": "Instead, as I mentioned in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.787,
          "end": 79.727,
          "en": "React Query by default passes some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.727,
          "end": 81.9,
          "en": "to your Query function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.9,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "So to fetch events in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 87.487,
          "en": "when assigned to Query FN like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.487,
          "end": 90,
          "en": "and the data it passes in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 92.49000000000001,
          "en": "is an object that gives us information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 94.68,
          "en": "about the Query key that was used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 98.432,
          "en": "for that Query and a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.432,
          "end": 103.35,
          "en": "And that signal is required for aborting that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.35,
          "end": 105.33,
          "en": "If you, for example, navigate away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.33,
          "end": 109.53,
          "en": "from this page before the request was finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "because React Query thankfully can do that for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "it can abort requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 118.44,
          "en": "and it does that with help of that signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.44,
          "end": 120.96,
          "en": "So for that reason to give you that signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 123.33,
          "en": "and to also give you that Query key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 124.59,
          "en": "which you might want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.59,
          "end": 126.84,
          "en": "in your data fetching function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.84,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "For that reason, React Query passes an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 133.98,
          "en": "to that function you defined as a Query function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.98,
          "end": 138.32999999999998,
          "en": "Therefore here we should actually accept such an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "and we can use object destructuring here to pull out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 146.34,
          "en": "the different things we will get here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 151.26,
          "en": "the signal because if we do so, we can actually make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "that the request that is being sent is aborted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "If React Query thinks that it should be aborted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 161.463,
          "en": "because we for example, left the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.39,
          "end": 164.31,
          "en": "For that we can use this signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.31,
          "end": 167.07,
          "en": "and pass it to the built-in fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.07,
          "end": 170.16,
          "en": "by adding a second argument to fetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 172.29,
          "en": "a configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.29,
          "end": 174.95,
          "en": "which takes a signal property and wants a signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.95,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "of that shape as React Query gives it to us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "so that the browser then can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "that aboard signal internally to stop this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 187.89,
          "en": "if it receives that signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.89,
          "end": 190.6,
          "en": "So that's one thing we can do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.6,
          "end": 193.17,
          "en": "but that's not all I wanna do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.17,
          "end": 195.87,
          "en": "because of course I still wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.87,
          "end": 198.723,
          "en": "that I do forward the search term.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "So therefore here in this object which we receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 206.97,
          "en": "in fetch events, we could pull out a second property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.97,
          "end": 210.45,
          "en": "with any name of our choice, for example, search term.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.45,
          "end": 212.57999999999998,
          "en": "And now we just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.57999999999998,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "that in find events section where I'm wrapping fetch events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 220.02,
          "en": "with an anonymous function like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.02,
          "end": 222.27,
          "en": "I'm passing an object to fetch events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.27,
          "end": 226.14,
          "en": "and I'm setting a property named search term",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 230.133,
          "en": "in that object which I'm doing here in this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.54,
          "end": 233.264,
          "en": "This makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.264,
          "end": 236.264,
          "en": "that this search term property exists here when it's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 240.54,
          "en": "Now to also forward that signal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.54,
          "end": 243.21,
          "en": "we can simply accept this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.21,
          "end": 245.7,
          "en": "here in this anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.7,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "because that's now the function that will actually be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 253.74,
          "en": "by React Query and therefore we'll get the signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.74,
          "end": 255.27,
          "en": "I even get auto completion here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.27,
          "end": 258.12,
          "en": "and can see that I get the signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 259.41,
          "en": "We can then simply set it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.41,
          "end": 262.383,
          "en": "as a key value pair in this object here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "And therefore now we have the highest degree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 269.97,
          "en": "of flexibility we can have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.97,
          "end": 271.83,
          "en": "We can wrap fetch events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.83,
          "end": 276,
          "en": "with an anonymous function to pass any data we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 279.42,
          "en": "via that object to fetch events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.42,
          "end": 282.12,
          "en": "and still get that data that's provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.12,
          "end": 287.12,
          "en": "to us by React Query, or we set this function directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.09000000000003,
          "end": 291.15,
          "en": "as a value for Query event if we're happy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.15,
          "end": 295.44,
          "en": "with the default object we're getting by React Query,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 295.44,
          "end": 296.61,
          "en": "which is the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.61,
          "end": 299.7,
          "en": "in New Events section where I don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.7,
          "end": 303.723,
          "en": "to pass any custom data to my data fetching function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.89,
          "end": 308.07,
          "en": "And therefore with that, if we set this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.07,
          "end": 312.39,
          "en": "the data is back here in recently added events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.39,
          "end": 316.26,
          "en": "and this find your next event area also still works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.26,
          "end": 320.49,
          "en": "as before, but we're now also going to take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.49,
          "end": 322.56,
          "en": "at how exactly it works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 325.563,
          "en": "and how we might want to change that behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}